{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The draft application is largely faithful to the inventor's disclosure, but I found two instances where specific structural details in the claims and description are not explicitly supported by the provided source materials. These details, while plausible engineering implementations, represent assertions of technical substance that are not found in the inventor's own words. Both are critical disclosure-fidelity findings that must be corrected before filing.\n\nThe first finding concerns a geometric detail of the sight notch claimed in claim 6. The claim recites that the notch \"opens through an end edge\" of the rail, but the source only states that the notch is formed \"in the second end,\" without this specific detail.\n\nThe second finding concerns the shape of the clamping shoe. Both claim 12 and the detailed description state that the shoe \"spans the longitudinal slot,\" a specific configuration that is not described in the source, which only places the shoe \"below the rail.\"\n\nBoth findings include a recommended fix to remove the unsupported language, thereby conforming the draft to the inventor's disclosure. The remainder of the application, including its formalities, terminology, internal consistency, and the support for its other claims and features, appears to be sound."}
